WEBVTT

00:14.203 --> 00:16.456
IKEBUKURO STATION

00:16.539 --> 00:17.957
<i>There's someone I want to see.</i>

00:25.882 --> 00:29.427
<i>I'm Taiki Inomata, a first-year student
at Eimei Private High School.</i>

00:31.429 --> 00:34.807
<i>I fell in love with Chinatsu Senpai,
who's in the grade above me.</i>

00:36.350 --> 00:39.145
She'll be living with us
starting this spring.

00:39.729 --> 00:41.022
Thanks for having me.

00:42.106 --> 00:45.151
I told Taiki that I like him.

00:45.860 --> 00:49.030
I can't be with you.

00:49.614 --> 00:52.158
A tracksuit!
I wanted to go buy a tracksuit!

00:52.241 --> 00:53.785
<i>It's a date!</i>

00:54.368 --> 00:57.997
<i>It's also my chance
to tell her how I feel.</i>

00:58.080 --> 01:01.375
<i>In front of the flower bed.</i>

01:24.482 --> 01:28.653
BLUE BOX SEASON 2

02:51.068 --> 02:52.486
SHINJUKU STATION

02:52.570 --> 02:55.573
EPISODE 26
DÉJÀ VU

03:11.881 --> 03:16.510
Would it be in the badminton section
or the apparel section?

03:20.222 --> 03:22.266
Come on, Taiki.
Let's go to the second floor.

03:22.350 --> 03:23.517
Okay.

03:28.606 --> 03:33.319
<i>This is the first time
that I was the one who invited her out.</i>

03:33.402 --> 03:36.781
<i>That makes this our first real date.</i>

03:37.406 --> 03:39.867
Do you want to go somewhere together
on our next day off?

03:39.951 --> 03:43.788
There's this café I'd like to check out.
Can we go there too?

03:43.871 --> 03:45.790
<i>A café!</i>

03:47.375 --> 03:49.293
<i>There are so many different sports.</i>

03:50.878 --> 03:54.048
<i>So many different kinds of sportswear!</i>

04:04.350 --> 04:07.395
<i>Crap, I'm getting carried away.</i>

04:07.478 --> 04:08.562
Taiki.

04:09.063 --> 04:11.315
SQUID

04:11.399 --> 04:12.984
What about this one?

04:15.444 --> 04:16.988
Are you being serious?

04:17.071 --> 04:18.322
Totally serious.

04:18.406 --> 04:21.117
- Would you wear it?
- Nope.

04:21.200 --> 04:23.369
Then why would you think <i>I</i> would?!

04:24.704 --> 04:25.955
It was worth a shot.

04:27.331 --> 04:29.375
BIG CATCH

04:31.335 --> 04:33.629
<i>I love how comfortable this feels!</i>

04:34.547 --> 04:35.381
Ta-da!

04:35.464 --> 04:36.424
CERTAIN VICTORY

04:37.717 --> 04:38.592
Ta-da!

04:38.676 --> 04:39.510
NICE TO MEOW YA!

04:41.721 --> 04:44.640
STRETCH

04:44.724 --> 04:46.976
Then what about this?

04:49.020 --> 04:50.396
Wait, I think I like this one.

04:52.231 --> 04:53.858
It looks cool.

04:56.068 --> 04:59.405
It comes in a bigger size
if you want to be safe.

05:03.075 --> 05:04.577
I'll take this one.

05:04.660 --> 05:07.330
Tracksuits are cool, aren't they?

05:08.247 --> 05:10.583
I think I might buy a T-shirt too.

05:11.125 --> 05:12.793
I'm gonna go try it on.

05:12.877 --> 05:13.711
Okay.

05:18.799 --> 05:22.720
<i>Is it okay for me to wait
right outside the fitting room?</i>

05:22.803 --> 05:26.307
<i>But she might come out to show me
once she puts it on.</i>

05:26.849 --> 05:29.352
<i>So I should stay close just in case.</i>

05:35.232 --> 05:37.026
<i>The size is perfect.</i>

05:38.235 --> 05:39.862
<i>I'll ask Taiki what he thinks.</i>

05:40.863 --> 05:41.864
Oh?

05:41.947 --> 05:44.116
Yo, Inomata!

05:44.700 --> 05:45.993
Yokomura...

05:46.077 --> 05:47.411
Funny running into you here.

05:47.495 --> 05:49.121
Are you here to buy volleyball gear?

05:51.457 --> 05:53.375
Women's shoes?

05:54.794 --> 05:56.420
Say no more.

05:56.504 --> 05:59.215
I never would've thought. Props, man.

05:59.298 --> 06:00.216
Good luck, fam.

06:00.299 --> 06:01.133
No, it's not...

06:01.801 --> 06:04.178
I'm gonna get out of your hair,
and I won't tell anyone.

06:04.261 --> 06:05.179
Thanks.

06:05.262 --> 06:08.140
I just want to confirm one thing.

06:08.766 --> 06:09.892
Is it Chono?

06:11.852 --> 06:12.895
What?

06:13.479 --> 06:15.648
Sorry, never mind. It's not cool to pry.

06:15.731 --> 06:16.607
Later, man.

06:17.983 --> 06:20.402
<i>So that's what people think?</i>

06:21.570 --> 06:23.155
<i>I mean, we were close.</i>

06:38.254 --> 06:39.338
<i>She's not wearing it.</i>

06:40.089 --> 06:41.132
How was it?

06:41.215 --> 06:43.968
It was a little too big.

06:44.468 --> 06:46.053
I see.

06:46.137 --> 06:48.806
I think I'll come back some other time.

06:48.889 --> 06:51.142
Okay. I'll go pay for this, then.

06:51.976 --> 06:53.894
I'm dying to go to that café.

06:54.812 --> 06:55.646
Yeah.

07:18.586 --> 07:19.962
It's close to here, right?

07:20.045 --> 07:23.799
Yeah. I went with Nagisa before.

07:23.883 --> 07:25.801
<i>So it's somewhere she's been before.</i>

07:26.469 --> 07:30.556
They had the best apple pie I've ever had.

07:31.307 --> 07:33.309
I want you to try it.

07:35.394 --> 07:38.355
In that case,
there's some food I'd like you to try too.

07:38.439 --> 07:39.815
We can do that next time.

07:41.317 --> 07:42.318
I'd like that.

07:50.868 --> 07:52.328
Welcome.

07:53.829 --> 07:54.705
Table for two--

07:57.041 --> 07:58.083
You're here by yourself?

07:58.167 --> 08:00.294
You could actually join us if you'd like.

08:00.377 --> 08:01.921
Matsuoka?

08:04.048 --> 08:05.591
Natsu!

08:08.886 --> 08:11.430
Meeting in a place like this,
it must be fate.

08:11.514 --> 08:12.723
This is stupid.

08:12.806 --> 08:16.727
Sit here, Natsu.
I mean, every other seat is taken, anyway.

08:17.311 --> 08:18.312
<i>What?</i>

08:20.481 --> 08:21.315
Aren't you that fan?

08:21.398 --> 08:24.985
It's Inomata.
I've been here the whole time!

08:26.362 --> 08:29.615
Wait, why are the two of you together?

08:33.744 --> 08:35.246
Not cool, Natsu.

08:35.329 --> 08:39.333
You shouldn't drag your fan here
just because you can't go to a café alone.

08:39.416 --> 08:41.377
I can go to cafes by myself just fine.

08:41.460 --> 08:43.420
Anyway, take a seat.

08:48.300 --> 08:49.885
<i>You know, at first,</i>

08:50.928 --> 08:53.472
<i>I thought this guy
was just a terrible person.</i>

08:53.556 --> 08:54.890
I need to use the restroom.

08:54.974 --> 08:58.394
<i>But maybe he's just a ditz
who can't read the room.</i>

09:04.817 --> 09:07.695
Hey, fanboy, now's your chance.

09:08.195 --> 09:09.029
What?

09:15.744 --> 09:17.663
<i>Nope.</i>

09:17.746 --> 09:22.167
<i>He really is the worst!</i>

09:25.087 --> 09:27.172
Sorry, do you not understand English?

09:27.756 --> 09:30.926
I was asking you nicely to leave.

09:31.010 --> 09:33.095
<i>Nicely? Pretty sure
that was the imperative form!</i>

09:34.638 --> 09:36.849
That's what I should be saying to you.

09:36.932 --> 09:41.103
I made plans to spend the day alone
with Chinatsu Senpai.

09:41.186 --> 09:43.314
- You're the one intruding--
- I'm back.

09:45.316 --> 09:47.026
Welcome back, Natsu.

09:47.109 --> 09:51.614
<i>Chinatsu Senpai, you have to see
through this guy's fake smile!</i>

09:51.697 --> 09:54.033
You've got that shady look
on your face again.

09:54.116 --> 09:55.367
That's so mean.

09:55.451 --> 09:57.369
<i>She already knows?!</i>

09:57.453 --> 09:58.787
What do you want to order, Natsu?

09:58.871 --> 10:00.164
Apple pie and tea.

10:00.247 --> 10:02.666
Right, you're a tea person.

10:02.750 --> 10:04.668
You're always drinking tea in class.

10:04.752 --> 10:06.920
Even I knew that!

10:07.004 --> 10:08.213
Excuse me!

10:08.297 --> 10:09.548
What are you ordering?

10:09.632 --> 10:10.674
I'll have...

10:11.342 --> 10:12.593
Protein?

10:12.676 --> 10:14.178
<i>The guy's making digs at me!</i>

10:15.262 --> 10:18.307
I'll also get the apple pie and tea
Chinatsu Senpai recommende--

10:18.390 --> 10:22.519
This reminds me
of that time in middle school.

10:22.603 --> 10:23.979
<i>Let me talk!</i>

10:24.063 --> 10:27.232
The whole basketball team
went to a café after practice.

10:27.316 --> 10:28.859
Are you ready to order?

10:28.942 --> 10:32.363
Could we get two of each of these, please?

10:32.446 --> 10:34.031
Of course.

10:34.114 --> 10:35.824
That brings back memories!

10:35.908 --> 10:38.202
We wanted to go somewhere fancy.

10:38.285 --> 10:39.370
We did, didn't we?

10:40.162 --> 10:43.374
Taiki, you know that cafe in Nichome?

10:43.957 --> 10:44.792
Oh, that one--

10:44.875 --> 10:48.128
It was pretty pricey
for a middle schooler's budget.

10:48.712 --> 10:51.757
Nagisa ordered an espresso
to try to look cool.

10:52.800 --> 10:54.510
No, that was Yumeka.

10:58.722 --> 10:59.723
<i>What was that?</i>

10:59.807 --> 11:03.769
Was it? Oh, but then there was
that whole thing on our way home...

11:03.852 --> 11:05.270
<i>Who's Yumeka?</i>

11:08.357 --> 11:09.983
Here is your order.

11:25.124 --> 11:28.293
<i>The harmony between the crispy crust
and the sweet apples!</i>

11:32.881 --> 11:34.216
Anyway...

11:36.718 --> 11:38.429
It's so good.

11:56.738 --> 11:58.073
Now, then...

11:59.491 --> 12:00.576
Where shall we go next?

12:02.286 --> 12:06.790
- Hey!
- Now that we've eaten, what about bowling?

12:08.917 --> 12:11.795
Sorry, I forgot something in the café.
I'll be right back.

12:15.299 --> 12:17.801
<i>We finally got some time alone together...</i>

12:30.230 --> 12:31.064
Sorry.

12:31.148 --> 12:33.108
<i>He's definitely doing that on purpose.</i>

12:33.192 --> 12:34.568
Listen.

12:35.819 --> 12:38.322
Do you really have time for romance?

12:45.037 --> 12:49.416
Didn't you
just lose to Haryu the other day?

12:49.500 --> 12:50.834
And it wasn't just to him.

12:51.418 --> 12:53.086
Plus, it doesn't look to me

12:53.170 --> 12:56.840
like you're much better
than your other teammates.

12:57.424 --> 13:00.511
Me, though, I'm super good at basketball,

13:00.594 --> 13:03.055
and it's easy for me
to balance sports and romance.

13:05.390 --> 13:06.808
I can manage both.

13:09.811 --> 13:11.063
Really?

13:16.443 --> 13:17.819
Sorry to keep you waiting!

13:18.320 --> 13:19.571
Not at all.

13:23.158 --> 13:25.869
<i>He hit me where it hurts.</i>

13:25.953 --> 13:27.704
<i>I can feel myself sweating.</i>

13:28.288 --> 13:31.833
<i>I've already decided
I wouldn't let unfounded fears</i>

13:32.459 --> 13:34.169
<i>hold me back anymore.</i>

13:34.670 --> 13:36.588
Anyway, Matsuoka...

13:36.672 --> 13:38.090
Hold on, I just got a text.

13:39.883 --> 13:41.635
This is perfect!

13:41.718 --> 13:46.223
Some people I know from Yusei University
are playing basketball right now.

13:46.306 --> 13:47.599
Let's go join them, Natsu!

13:48.183 --> 13:49.184
What?

13:52.312 --> 13:55.065
Yusei University
has a strong basketball team,

13:55.148 --> 13:56.858
so you could learn a lot.

13:57.484 --> 13:58.860
But...

14:00.654 --> 14:03.532
They told me to bring anyone.

14:04.950 --> 14:06.493
You should go!

14:09.329 --> 14:12.666
You'll learn a lot
practicing with college students!

14:14.001 --> 14:16.003
Don't worry about me!

14:16.587 --> 14:19.756
Besides, I'm gonna go home
and get some practice in too!

14:23.343 --> 14:24.720
You heard the guy.

14:24.803 --> 14:26.263
Come on, let's go!

14:27.556 --> 14:29.975
- Let's go.
- But...

14:30.058 --> 14:31.685
This way.

14:33.186 --> 14:34.479
Later!

14:35.606 --> 14:37.482
I didn't do it for you!

14:57.377 --> 15:00.213
<i>I wanted to keep hanging out with her,</i>

15:03.800 --> 15:06.637
<i>but I want to support her
in basketball too.</i>

15:09.139 --> 15:11.516
<i>And me butting heads with that Matsu guy...</i>

15:16.605 --> 15:18.982
<i>won't do her any good.</i>

15:45.884 --> 15:48.095
I thought you got on that train.

15:48.595 --> 15:50.097
I went to the bathroom.

15:51.974 --> 15:54.601
What about that basketball practice?

15:57.813 --> 16:01.358
After thinking it over, I realized
I didn't have a change of clothes.

16:08.573 --> 16:10.409
Then let's go home together!

16:14.496 --> 16:15.747
<i>I'm so happy.</i>

16:16.415 --> 16:18.250
<i>Happy that she came back.</i>

16:18.750 --> 16:20.585
<i>Happy we get to go home together.</i>

16:21.837 --> 16:25.924
<i>But as happy as I am,
there's a lot that I have to do.</i>

16:26.842 --> 16:28.635
Nagisa Senpai.

16:29.428 --> 16:31.805
I found this picture while cleaning.

16:31.888 --> 16:33.890
Who's the person wearing number four?

16:33.974 --> 16:35.559
Oh, her?

16:36.476 --> 16:37.894
Yumeka Kido.

16:41.773 --> 16:44.609
The apple pie was good, wasn't it?

16:44.693 --> 16:46.319
Best I've ever had!

16:47.446 --> 16:48.780
I'm glad to hear that.

16:48.864 --> 16:50.824
The day went by so fast.

16:51.575 --> 16:53.410
It did, didn't it?

16:53.910 --> 16:56.329
NEXT STOP - OMOTESANDO

16:57.956 --> 16:59.332
Chinatsu Senpai.

16:59.416 --> 17:02.586
What do you think
about staying out a little longer?

17:09.676 --> 17:13.722
<i>I know a perfect spot
for this time of day.</i>

17:27.444 --> 17:28.945
It's beautiful.

17:29.654 --> 17:31.615
We came at a good time.

17:32.866 --> 17:36.119
Yeah, it's like time is in slow motion.

17:38.121 --> 17:39.873
<i>I wish time would stop!</i>

17:42.709 --> 17:44.544
It really is beautiful.

17:44.628 --> 17:45.921
It sure is.

17:52.677 --> 17:54.137
But I'm a little surprised.

17:54.221 --> 17:55.138
What?

17:55.222 --> 17:58.517
I didn't think
you would know about spots like this.

17:59.726 --> 18:00.977
I mean...

18:01.061 --> 18:03.063
HIGH SCHOOLER - DATE - NIGHT VIEW

18:03.146 --> 18:03.980
OUTING

18:04.064 --> 18:06.066
<i>I did tons of research
after we made plans!</i>

18:06.149 --> 18:08.276
- Don't tell me...
- Yes?

18:09.569 --> 18:10.862
You came here with another girl?

18:10.946 --> 18:13.240
Of course not!

18:13.323 --> 18:15.826
I mean, this is my first time here,

18:15.909 --> 18:18.745
and I was worried
we'd get lost on the way here.

18:26.169 --> 18:28.505
This is my first time here too.

18:29.923 --> 18:34.594
Until today, I thought
that hanging out was like slacking off.

18:36.930 --> 18:38.265
<i>Who is Yumeka?</i>

18:38.348 --> 18:41.768
I guess you wouldn't know
if you joined Eimei in high school.

18:43.603 --> 18:47.274
What? You can't even do that?

18:47.357 --> 18:49.776
You wouldn't know
about Yumeka's Spartan training

18:49.860 --> 18:51.027
and her sarcastic attitude!

18:52.612 --> 18:54.531
But she was a genius.

18:55.448 --> 18:57.242
<i>She and Chinatsu had great chemistry</i>

18:57.325 --> 18:59.661
<i>since they'd been playing together
from a young age.</i>

18:59.744 --> 19:00.745
AWARD

19:01.371 --> 19:02.622
I see.

19:02.706 --> 19:03.540
But...

19:03.623 --> 19:06.168
Yeah, she quit in middle school.

19:07.252 --> 19:08.920
<i>Without saying a word.</i>

19:09.963 --> 19:12.424
She quit our school and basketball too.

19:23.185 --> 19:24.728
Are you cold?

19:24.811 --> 19:26.438
No, I'm fine.

19:28.899 --> 19:30.358
Here, put this on.

19:30.942 --> 19:34.070
The tracksuit I just bought
should help block the wind.

19:34.779 --> 19:37.240
I should also have
some hand warmers somewhere.

19:37.324 --> 19:39.075
Mom made me bring them.

19:39.159 --> 19:42.662
They should be in this pocket...

19:47.292 --> 19:48.710
What is it?

19:51.922 --> 19:54.090
It just felt like déjà vu.

19:57.469 --> 20:00.764
Hey! Use this if you like!

20:00.847 --> 20:02.349
It's just been washed!

20:03.975 --> 20:06.686
And... here's some hot tea.

20:06.770 --> 20:09.314
This thermos is great
at keeping things warm.

20:09.397 --> 20:11.900
Here are some gloves, and a pocket heater!

20:12.484 --> 20:14.152
It gets warm if you shake...

20:17.489 --> 20:19.824
Looking back, it must've been creepy.

20:19.908 --> 20:23.954
Suddenly having this underclassman
you don't know pushing his scarf on you.

20:24.037 --> 20:25.497
Honestly, I was startled.

20:25.580 --> 20:26.414
What?

20:29.918 --> 20:32.170
But I didn't find it creepy.

20:33.213 --> 20:37.217
Because even if I had never talked
to you before, I saw you every morning.

20:42.472 --> 20:44.933
I already knew you must be

20:45.016 --> 20:49.145
a really honest and hardworking person
with integrity.

20:58.488 --> 21:00.991
What will you bring me next?

21:10.375 --> 21:11.501
Just kidding.

21:17.882 --> 21:19.718
I don't have anything to give you,

21:19.801 --> 21:21.094
but...

21:22.929 --> 21:25.223
there's something I want to tell you.

21:27.934 --> 21:29.311
Natsu?

21:38.069 --> 21:39.487
Yumeka.

21:40.572 --> 21:42.365
<i>Wait, that name came up before.</i>

21:43.491 --> 21:44.993
What?

21:45.076 --> 21:47.996
Is this for real?

21:48.663 --> 21:50.999
You got a boyfriend too?

21:51.082 --> 21:53.752
No, I'm not her boyfriend.

21:55.170 --> 21:56.254
I see.

21:57.839 --> 22:00.759
The only thing you ever cared about
was basketball.

22:00.842 --> 22:03.595
To think that Natsu is dating.

22:08.558 --> 22:09.976
So I guess...

22:12.145 --> 22:14.981
you must have
given up on basketball, then.

23:48.950 --> 23:53.955
Subtitle translation by: Zensho Yamamoto
